From 8446e587194a9c1511dee28ab60ee603052b5215 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 13:45:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00918/11362] [outer-loop] clean 4096 RFT verdict:
 verifier-as-reward NO CLEAR LIFT, doesn't beat SC (math)

Truncation-valid 3-seed on-policy RFT (eval max_new=4096, all seeds trunc_ok, gold control
passes all). Verdict: no_clear_lift.
  gold              +0.271 +/-0.048  [0.33,0.24,0.25]  lower1sig +0.223  -> robust, TEACHES
  process_weighted  +0.033 +/-0.081  [0.08,0.08,-0.06] lower1sig -0.048  -> NOT clean
  sc_weighted       +0.042 +/-0.045  [0.03,0.09,0.01]  lower1sig -0.003  -> NOT clean
  process_plus_sc   +0.044 +/-0.100                                       -> NOT clean
  unweighted        -0.011                                                -> hurts

Findings: (1) gold-RFT decisively teaches -> mechanism sound. (2) verifier-as-reward does NOT
cleanly teach (seed2 negative under clean eval; the flagged-1024 +0.08/+0.15 did not survive).
(3) verifier does NOT beat self-consistency (process_weighted ~ sc_weighted, SC lower-variance)
-> MOAT REFUTED for the RFT-reward use in MATH. Root cause: math is SC-near-ceiling (no headroom)
-> reinforces the pivot to ARC, where the verifier's value is real (arc_grid_combined_verifier v2).
Registry: outcome_verifier_math_proc_plus_sc marked DO-NOT-PROMOTE (causal RFT negative).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
